<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  rd.xml - hand-written runtime directives for ILC.

  This file is deliberately almost empty. Two things had to be learned the
  hard way to get here, and both are worth stating so they are not
  reintroduced:

  1. ILC's rd.xml support is a SUBSET of the old .NET Native runtime
     directives. It accepts <Assembly> and <Type> (with <Method>, <Field>,
     <Property>, <Event> beneath them). It does NOT accept <Namespace>, and
     reports "Namespace is not a supported Runtime Directive" as a hard
     failure. Six MegaCrit.Sts2.Core.* namespace roots used to live here.

  2. An <Assembly Name="X"> naming an assembly that is not in the compilation
     is also a HARD ERROR - "Failed to load assembly 'X'" - not something ILC
     skips. GodotSharpEditor (editor-only), System.Text.Json, FmodSharp,
     fmod_godot, spine-godot and SpineGodotSharp were all named here and each
     failed the build in turn.

  So the assembly roots are GENERATED into rd.generated.xml by
  scripts/docker-entry.sh, from the assemblies actually being fed to ILC. That
  list cannot drift from reality, and rooting all of them is the intent anyway
  (see aot/README.md: start broad, narrow once the game boots).

  What the namespace roots were FOR still matters. ModelDb.Init builds the
  whole content database by reflecting over AllAbstractModelSubtypes, so every
  model type must survive trimming with its metadata and a callable
  constructor. That is now covered by the generated
  <Assembly Name="sts2" Dynamic="Required All" />, which roots the assembly
  those namespaces live in.

  If the build ever needs to be narrowed from "root all of sts2" to something
  smaller, this is where the <Type> entries go - one per type, since
  <Namespace> is not available. Check the ModelDb phase-1/phase-2 counts in
  sts2_debug.log against a desktop run before and after any such change; a
  trimmed model type does not throw, it just quietly disappears from the
  content database.
-->
<Directives xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/netfx/2013/01/metadata">
  <Application>
  </Application>
</Directives>
